    narr:generatedFrom "940612e45daea4f69021c82a442a37e720a8a507" ;
    narr:narration """On 2026-08-06, Quinton Fairweather issued a mandatory gate: [every Meridian deployment now requires a signed release manifest](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1) before shipping. The justification cited is a concrete provenance failure — [two unsigned artifacts reached staging last quarter](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2), which Fairweather names as \"the whole reason for the gate.\" The decision is restated in editorial voice by XenaExpertgh as a [gate requiring signed manifests for Meridian deploys](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_3), with [scope covering both staging and production](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4) and [ownership assigned to Quinton Fairweather](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5). The mandate's reach is thus broader than a single environment, and its ownership is singular rather than distributed. The cited incident is narrow — two artifacts, one quarter — yet the response is a standing precondition across two deployment tiers. No dissent or qualification appears among the children; the gate is presented as settled. The register splits between Fairweather's plain-spoken justification and the editorial restatement's matter-of-fact technical phrasing.""" ;
